From 4d5c571c85a29e478ed2e2716b5e72c19b7d7486 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AzediZ <145237384+AzediZ@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 20:30:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Sovereignty: zero the empty result for systems with no sov
 data

SovereigntyDataMgr::GetSovereigntyData() returned an uninitialised SovereigntyData when the
system had no sov entry (all of empire space), so jammerID, beaconID and the rest were
garbage. Cynos then refused to light anywhere outside claimed null-sec with "This system is
currently being jammed", and the same garbage reached jump bridge onlining and structure
anchoring checks.
---
 src/eve-server/system/sov/SovereigntyDataMgr.cpp | 5 +++--
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/eve-server/system/sov/SovereigntyDataMgr.cpp b/src/eve-server/system/sov/SovereigntyDataMgr.cpp
index a6908eb..2f99f73 100644
--- a/src/eve-server/system/sov/SovereigntyDataMgr.cpp
+++ b/src/eve-server/system/sov/SovereigntyDataMgr.cpp
@@ -118,8 +118,9 @@ SovereigntyData SovereigntyDataMgr::GetSovereigntyData(uint32 systemID)
         return sData;
     } else
     {
-        //Return empty object in case we don't find anything
-        SovereigntyData sData;
+        //Return empty object in case we don't find anything.  zeroed: a plain 'SovereigntyData sData;' left jammerID, beaconID
+        // and the rest as garbage, so every system without sov data (all of empire space) looked jammed to cynos
+        SovereigntyData sData = SovereigntyData();
         return sData;
     }
 }
